# --- workshop — stays on disk, never pushed to public ---
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH ON ANY LOCAL-STATE ENTRY, anywhere in this file.
#
# A trailing slash matches directories only. An opencode worktree represents
# `node_modules`, `.claude` and `.opencode` as symlinks to the main checkout, and
# a symlink is not a directory — so `node_modules/` does not match it, and
# `git add -A` commits the link with its absolute local path inside. That has
# happened once (commit 6b5523c). On a machine where core.symlinks=false, git
# then checks those links out as plain files, which REPLACES the real directory
# it pointed at. Directory-only patterns are still correct for generated content
# below (build/, src/generated/, output/, docs/, ...), where a file of that name
# must not be ignored by accident.
.claude
.opencode
.reasonix
.vscode
.mimocode
.freebuff
.gstack
.ula
output/
docs/
design-plans/
research/
data/contrib/
tmp
uncited.txt
uncited2.txt

